Disable nvmath's numba-cuda backend

nvmath gates its numba-cuda backend on `find_spec("numba.cuda")`, which cannot
express "numba-cuda is absent". With no numba installed the probe raises
ModuleNotFoundError, making nvmath.device unimportable; with numba installed it
matches numba's own `numba/cuda` shim and nvmath then fails importing the
backend modules. This CI job installs neither - it exercises only the
numba-cuda-mlir backend - so pin the gate off.

TODO: drop once nvmath-python probes for numba-cuda itself.

Context is kept to one line so the patch survives edits elsewhere in the file.
Applied by ci/tools/run-nvmath-python-mlir-tests.

diff --git a/nvmath/device/common.py b/nvmath/device/common.py
--- a/nvmath/device/common.py
+++ b/nvmath/device/common.py
@@ -15,3 +15,3 @@ from .common_cuda import MAX_SUPPORTED_CC, MIN_SUPPORTED_CC, CodeType, ComputeCa

-_HAS_NUMBA = importlib.util.find_spec("numba.cuda") is not None
+_HAS_NUMBA = False
 _HAS_NUMBA_CUDA_MLIR = importlib.util.find_spec("numba_cuda_mlir") is not None
